                        ],
                        "form": "logiciens"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "408e7816-c831-47f7-b176-81b4de98ba61",
                        "entry_id": "ac987dae-84a3-390c-851a-2d806afe1bda",
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "logicienne"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d182052-f167-37c3-bf54-0ec34123fcfa",
                        "entry_id": "ac987dae-84a3-390c-851a-2d806afe1bda",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Spécialiste de la logique en tant que discipline."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f5568e7-f95f-4f87-967d-5a32adaab06f",
                                "sense_id": "9d182052-f167-37c3-bf54-0ec34123fcfa",
                                "text": "Le but des logiciens n'est donc pas tant de résoudre des problèmes mais plutôt d'expliquer la manière dont les autres résolvent ces problèmes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99d2b381-f45b-4da7-8705-1c623feae428",
                                "sense_id": "9d182052-f167-37c3-bf54-0ec34123fcfa",
                                "text": "Certes, Libavius (1560-1616), dans son célèbre Alchemia de 1597, s'applique à traiter clairement et méthodiquement d'une science qu'il juge embarrassée d'obscurités inutiles et use ainsi de la taxinomie arborescente du logicien Pierre La Ramée (1515-1572) pour organiser la matière de son ouvrage."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e3a9ba5-00ef-399a-a7a0-514cb70bc69d",
                        "entry_id": "ac987dae-84a3-390c-851a-2d806afe1bda",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Spécialiste de la logique informatique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e163bb3a-669a-37af-81b4-0644eceadfb7",
                        "entry_id": "ac987dae-84a3-390c-851a-2d806afe1bda",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne qui raisonne avec justesse et méthode."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc6e460a-b169-4068-aa9b-002cc1c41bb0",
                                "sense_id": "e163bb3a-669a-37af-81b4-0644eceadfb7",
                                "text": "Vous raisonnez en bon logicien."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ac8d2b8-52ca-4307-aea0-939ea6b4e03c",
                                "sense_id": "e163bb3a-669a-37af-81b4-0644eceadfb7",
                                "text": "Ils recomposaient, à l’usage du juge, une histoire simple, fortement liée et qui pût satisfaire ce logicien."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1f41bc2c-5a13-4566-ac97-e2ac35ca5dc9",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac987dae-84a3-390c-851a-2d806afe1bda",
                        "target_lang_word": "logician",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "logician",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f3ee3bc-0471-31e8-a0f7-3ecaca229206",
                                        "entry_id": "5f0b4cbe-a62c-37e6-aab7-83f958addb5b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who studies or teaches logic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d567050-5084-4953-8489-245f7cabb325",
                                                "sense_id": "0f3ee3bc-0471-31e8-a0f7-3ecaca229206",
                                                "text": "“To the logician all things should be seen exactly as they are.” ― “The Greek Interpreter”, by Sir Arthur Conan Doyle, 1894"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86077b2c-15ad-4b79-85bc-690c9d709958",
                                                "sense_id": "0f3ee3bc-0471-31e8-a0f7-3ecaca229206",
                                                "text": "It is not unknown for a logician to talk about exes and wyes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aabe3a41-21a7-4eb0-9f9f-40e52b645ff2",
                                                "sense_id": "0f3ee3bc-0471-31e8-a0f7-3ecaca229206",
                                                "text": "These two treatments of the predicate are typical of the two traditions in traditional logic—the intensional and the extensional traditions. Logicians who can be counted among the intensional logicians are Gottfried Leibniz, Johann Lambert, William Hamilton, Stanley Jevons, and Hugh MacColl. Among the extensional logicians are George Boole, Augustus De Morgan, Charles Peirce, and John Venn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
